    <h3>
        <u><a style="color: black" name="hipaa-and-phi"> HIPAA and PHI</a></u>
    </h3>
    <p>
        Certain demographic, health and/or health-related information that
        NuviDoc collects about Users on behalf of our Healthcare Providers as
        part of providing the Services may be &ldquo;protected health
        information&rdquo; (&ldquo;PHI&rdquo;) governed by the Health Insurance
        Portability and Accountability Act (&ldquo;HIPAA&rdquo;). Specifically,
        this may be true when (i) NuviDoc is providing administrative,
        operational, or other services to a Healthcare Provider that is a
        &ldquo;Covered Entity&rdquo; (as defined by HIPAA); and (ii) in order to
        provide those services, NuviDoc receives identifiable information about a
        User on behalf of the Healthcare Provider, where NuviDoc is acting as a
        &ldquo;Business Associate&rdquo; (as defined by HIPAA); and (iii) this
        identifiable information is regulated as PHI.
    </p>
    <p>
        <span style="font-weight: 700">
            This Privacy Policy does not apply to PHI, which is instead
            regulated by HIPAA.
        </span>
        HIPAA provides specific protections for the privacy and security of PHI
        and restricts how PHI is used and disclosed. Please read the Notice of
        Privacy Practices of your Healthcare Provider to understand how your PHI
        can be used and disclosed.
    </p>
    <p>
        Personal data that a User provides to NuviDoc when NuviDoc is not acting
        as a Business Associate is not PHI and NuviDoc&rsquo;s use of this
        information is therefore covered by this Privacy Policy. To provide just
        a few examples, we are collecting Personal Data when you: (i) create an
        account, (ii) search for Healthcare Providers or available appointments
        with Healthcare Providers; (iii) post reviews; (iv) provide device/IP
        Information or Web Analytics information by browsing our websites (see
        below); or (v) direct your Covered Entity healthcare provider to
        disclose PHI to NuviDoc outside of its Business Associate capacity (e.g.
        pursuant to a HIPAA Authorization or access request).
    </p>

    <h3>
